Widescreen ranges for side-on paths, and scenery across path ends.

Reported after 0049/0050: objects and scenery still pop in at the edges in
side-scrolling scenes (bonus rounds, Snow Go). Measured on the disc:

- Camera paths of kind 3 (and 8, property 0x029) look at the play from the
  side. Every object on them appears where its offset along the path from the
  camera is 0.94-2.3x its distance off the path (median 1.1) and vanishes at
  the mirror value: the 4:3 frame's side edges. A 16:9 frame sees each one
  a third of that offset earlier: 5-7 nodes typically, past 14 for some. The
  fixed window (k = 2) covered 1% of them.
- Paths are short (26-30 nodes) and joined end to end (1,815 of 1,990 at both
  ends), so long windows mostly stopped at a path's end.

crash2_wide_geom.h (new, read only): resident-entry lookup as 0x80014B90 does
it, the property accessor's search, path points, object positions (draw-list
value -> entity, checked on all 53,862 values), camera links (0x109, all
3,837 checked), zone world tables. 27 code words checked.

crash2_wide_spawn.h: on side-on paths each object's own reach, from its
position where the original starts or stops showing it (k elsewhere; never
less than k, at most 24 nodes; load/unload rules unchanged).

crash2_wide_slst.h: on side-on paths a per-path window, the 90th percentile of
its objects' reaches (met 98% of their needs; 7 nodes at 16:9 without enough
objects; at most 20), with up to as many polygons again as the game's list.
Past either end the window continues into the linked path's lists, world
slots remapped by EID to the current zone's (the renderer's), unmapped
polygons dropped.

New counters: wide_spawn side / side_miss; wide_slst side / joined / kw.
No file here is in codegen_hash_sources.cmake; overlay shards are unaffected.

